{"text": " You wake up in 1971 in a suburb of Pittsburgh. It's a Sunday evening in August and the whole family's in front of the TV. Did you know that in 1971, it was illegal for most Americans to own gold coins or bars? It had been since 1933. Gold was for governments. Since 1944, they could swap dollars for American gold at $35 an ounce. The dollar was tied to gold and most other money was tied to the dollar. That evening, President Nixon comes on. From now on, foreign governments can't swap their dollars for gold within a few years the whole system's gone. So what is money now? A promise backed by trust. Trust in the people who run it. And a generation later that trust takes a new shape. Money doesn't need paper at all. In Kenya, it moves into a text message.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.0, "text": " You wake up in 1971 in a suburb of Pittsburgh.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 34578, 294, 257, 1422, 16659, 295, 33626, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12439002338637653, "compression_ratio": 1.5440613026819923, "no_speech_prob": 0.005172418896108866, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.6076317429542542}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9653046131134033}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9986464381217957}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.992885172367096}, {"word": " 1971", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.34, "probability": 0.9911606907844543}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.34, "end": 2.06, "probability": 0.8822970986366272}, {"word": " a", "start": 2.06, "end": 2.14, "probability": 0.9878344535827637}, {"word": " suburb", "start": 2.14, "end": 2.5, "probability": 0.7653200626373291}, {"word": " of", "start": 2.5, "end": 2.66, "probability": 0.9221692085266113}, {"word": " Pittsburgh.", "start": 2.66, "end": 3.0, "probability": 0.9822972416877747}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.56, "end": 4.88, "text"